  "proof_scope": [
    "The exact actual Picard energy telescope gives the projected-average mean budget B=W+(1-sqrt(c))^2*(1-1/n)/T, tending to 1+tau+1/T. Mean/sector/mark-preserving nonnegative completion would give a direct ordinary-theta squeeze, without requiring conic o(kappa), UI or HR on this constructive route. No such prime-uniform completion is proved.",
    "For growing depth, the stated Cesaro squared-mark condition includes time T+1. The square prescribed averaged minus mark is infeasible when tau+1/T<1 (fixed depth) or tau<1 under the growing-depth hypotheses.",
    "The saved q151321 depth48 minus mark exceeds its exact feasible maximum 195 by a positive exact rational. All mean-one minus-sector nonnegative completions preserving this mark are impossible. This is stronger than one repair rejection and is not conic infeasibility.",
    "Five finite theta intervals and marked-gap comparisons are derived from accepted round34 exact-input positive certificates. No new large positivity transform is run for them; the new averaged positivity observations are floating only.",
    "Actual quadratic-profile signed spill has a sharp dimension-independent limit. The first nonscalar nested affine correction family retains normalized mark cap mu/sqrt(2), uniformly for field-dependent coefficients and with positive-density obstruction. These use only the accepted first-three-field compact law and do not identify later clipped deficits.",
    "The inherited mixed Mellin norm proves a common hot complex domain Re(tau)>0,1024<abs(tau)<n with coordinatewise nonzero actual reciprocal spectra and marked log bound 4/sqrt(n). It does not reach cold floors.",
    "An explicit cold weighted-barrier disk is proved. Tangent-rank trace forces only this full-Hessian isotropic certificate to shrink as n^(-1/2); no singularity at that distance is asserted.",
    "Exact actual p13 jets exclude global upper-half-plane Pick/Stieltjes representations of the specified observables in either direction, not right-half-plane holomorphy.",
    "A common square-family marked-log extension would require polynomially growing unwrapped phase. Subpolynomial prime phase on a common cold-hot domain would suffice, but neither is established.",
    "First-inverse source tightness gives sector-preserving bounded-energy affine L1 approximants with error sqrt(Delta/tau), potentially signed and still source-dependent. Exact positive-floor regularization retains an unknown distributed forcing, so the original inverse arithmetic bridge remains open.",
    "All written proofs are ordinary mathematical audits, not Lean kernel verification. The 74 floating diagnostics are not stationary enclosures or asymptotic positivity evidence."
  ],
